and close refuses on that failure (V8).\"\n\nHmm, \"the verifier fails a record whose flags ... disagree with the ledger and logs\". Wait — does this imply the flag IS verified? Let me read carefully. \"The listing is not disclosure-only: the verifier fails a record whose flags lack the allowance or disagree with the ledger and logs (`allowance`, `hand-time-unflagged`, `flag-without-source`)\".\n\nThe three kinds: `allowance` — allowances.hand_times is present whenever hand-time set is non-empty (presence check, not verification of the time itself). `hand-time-unflagged` — a hand time the verifier recomputes... is missing from hand_times[] (i.e., all hand times must be flagged — this is a completeness check of the flags, not verification of the flagged time values). `flag-without-source` — a flag has no hand line behind it (checks the flag corresponds to an actual hand time).\n\nSo \"disagree with the ledger and logs\" here refers to: flags that should exist but don't (hand-time-unflagged), or flags that exist without backing hand lines (flag-without-source), or the allowance metadata. These checks ensure the flags are complete and honest — they don't verify the flagged time value itself. But the phrasing \"disagree with the ledger and logs\" could be read as implying the verifier checks the flagged time against the ledger and logs, which would be a form of verification... Hmm.\n\nActually wait, let me think about this more carefully in the context of the rule: \"it never verifies them, and a flagged time is not presented as checked, verified or trustworthy.\"\n\nLine 144-146 says \"The listing is not disclosure-only: the verifier fails a record whose flags lack the allowance or disagree with the ledger and logs\". The `hand-time-unflagged` kind at line 84: \"a hand time the verifier recomputes from the ledger, `inputs/custody.json`, or a server-time log call is missing from `x-plumbline.hand_times[]`.\" So the verifier recomputes which times are hand times and chec