                "text": "Let me analyze the document against the five rules.\n\n**Rule 1: Hand-entered times (times no tool stamped) are REFUSED by default.**\n\nLooking for lines saying hand times are refused by default:\n- Line 96-97: \"A time with no tool-written ledger line or logger time behind it is a **hand time**: refused by default\"\n- Line 103: \"a hand time (`inputs-no-ledger`): refused by default\"\n- Line 109: \"a hand time: refused by default\"\n- Line 130: \"## Hand times: refused by default, flagged under the switch\"\n- Line 137: \"**Hand times are refused by default.** With no switch, the emitter exits 3 with kind `hand-time`...\"\n- Line 350: \"a typed value is a hand time (refused unless --allow-hand-times)\"\n- Line 45: \"This includes every hand time when `--allow-hand-times` is not given (`hand-time`)\"\n\nThis is clearly stated. Rule 1 conforms.\n\n**Rule 2: The `--allow-hand-times` switch only FLAGS hand-entered times; it never verifies them, and a flagged time is not presented as checked/verified/trustworthy.**\n\n- Line 97: \"with `--allow-hand-times` flagged in `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` and never verified\"\n- Line 103: \"under `--allow-hand-times` flagged and never verified\"\n- Line 141-143: \"**The switch flags hand times and never verifies them.** `--allow-hand-times` does not check the time against a log or a clock. It records each hand time in `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` and, when the set is non-empty, writes `x-plumbline.allowances.hand_times = ...`.\"\n- Line 105-106: \"flagged under the switch, never verified\"\n- Line 109: \"flagged under the switch, never verified\"\n- Line 350: \"(refused unless --allow-hand-times)\" — flags.\n\nIs there anything that implies a flagged time is presented as checked/verified/trustworthy? Line 144-145: \"The listing is not disclosure-only: the verifier fails a record whose flags lack the allowance or disagree with the ledger and logs (`allowance`, `hand-time-unflagged`, `flag-without-source`), a